{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs1SSALSZN89oEmYt4Lm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `jsonpatch/core.py` per the spec and added `tests/test_core.py`. All 76 tests pass.\n\nThe cases the tests cover include:\n- **Atomic apply:** the input document is never mutated unless `in_place=True` and the patch succeeds. A failed patch leaves it unchanged either way.\n- **Move:** the \"into its own child\" check compares pointer tokens, not strings, so moving `/a` to `/ab` works. Moving a path onto itself does nothing, but `from` must still exist.\n- **Test operation:** `1 == 1.0` passes and `True != 1` fails, including inside nested lists and dicts.\n- **Malformed input:** bad patch shapes, unknown ops, missing fields and wrong types all raise `PatchError`.\n\nI made some choices where the spec was silent:\n- `remove` on the root (`\"\"`) raises `PatchError`.\n- When `in_place=True` and the root is replaced with a different type, the original can't be mutated. In that case the new document is returned.\n- A leading-zero array index like `01` is rejected, and the digit check is ASCII-only, so non-ASCII digits are rejected too."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1164,"cache_read_input_tokens":38958,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1164},"output_tokens":384,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8924f088-8123-4441-9749-121bd259af7d","uuid":"3ff70ef5-0e07-472c-a284-a1a004ee13a0","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:50:56.071Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs1SRsEgGk7nV5h7aCPX"}
